\f0\fs24 \cf0 Sauber Mercedes C9 v 1.1\
\
My interpretation of the Sauber Mercedes C9. This model is based on the 1989 World Sports Car Championship and Le Mans winning version. Jean-Louis Schlesser won the championship, with C9 drivers filling the next three places in the points table. The first three colour schemes are based on the cars used at Le Mans.\
\
Now updated to 1.1 for Redline 1.0.4.\
\
This version has specs to suit the Sprint configuration but still looks like the Le Mans version. Downforce is increased by approximately 250% to realistic levels, drag is also higher to suit the downforce and gearing is reduced to take advantage of it all. \
\
Now you can get 
\f1\i closer
\f0\i0  to the fastest lap speeds at Brands Hatch (1'16.1) and Spa Francorchamp (2'07.8) for 1989.\
